atlas surface

architecture civic-transparency
  canonical_name CivicTransparency
  family surface
  domain Surface / Civic records
  layer surface
  semantic_question What does the public record say about license plate reader cameras in North Texas towns -- how many are mapped per town, what councils voted on, how a resident asks for the rest -- without ever holding where one camera stands or where one car went?
  purpose An original civic transparency site (Who Watches the Road, site program civic-watch) built from ForeignTwin receipts by civic-ledger and written with the documented `bonfyre-web-address site` verbs, styled by its own presentation template. Six standing pages (cameras, council votes, ask your city, search logs, sources, fix something) and a dated front page that doubles as the correction log.
  maturity implemented
  consumes ForeignObservation
  consumes SitePresentation
  publishes CivicRecordPage
  node_types TownReaderCount
  node_types CouncilAgendaItem
  node_types SourceRead
  node_types CorrectionMessage
  state_types read
  state_types refused
  state_types failed_kept_previous
  internal_calculus civic-ledger towns: Overpass statistics elements only; any positional key refuses the whole body; a town crossing county lines is counted once
  internal_calculus civic-ledger council: Legistar matters deduplicated by MatterId, kept only when the title names a reader system or its vendor, first title line only, newest first, linked back to the city's LegislationDetail page
  internal_calculus civic-ledger reads: every read attempted, including robots refusals and server errors, as a table on the Sources page
  internal_calculus build.sh observe: a failed re-read never replaces the last usable receipt
  invariant a body is parsed only when its receipt says robots allowed the read, the source answered 200 and the bytes still hash to content_sha256
  invariant no element with lat, lon, center, geometry, bounds, nodes or members is ever accepted; the site counts by town and county only
  invariant a registration or plate-display ordinance that merely says "license plate" is not listed as a reader item
  invariant corrections arrive through the site's contact page into the owner's inbox; nothing a visitor sends is published automatically, and sender names are never published
  invariant every generated page names its source and the day it was read; OpenStreetMap counts carry ODbL attribution
  forbidden_inference a mapped reader count -> the number of cameras a city operates; it is volunteer-mapped and unconfirmed
  forbidden_inference an agenda item -> an executed contract or a current deployment; check the item's status and the city's own page
  forbidden_inference a council absent from the page -> that the city has no readers; its agenda service may have failed or live elsewhere
  forbidden_inference robots allowing a read -> a licence to republish beyond the stated terms (ODbL attribution, public record)
  forbidden_inference this site -> a tool for locating, avoiding or tracking a camera, a vehicle or a person; it holds none of that and will not offer a plate lookup
  forbidden_inference a site built in a fixture home -> a site published to the internet; placement on a live host is a human step
  source_path cmd/BonfyreSourceFrontier/tools/civic_ledger.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreSourceFrontier/tests/civic_ledger_test.sh
  source_path cmd/BonfyreSourceFrontier/Makefile
  source_path docs/experiences/civic-transparency/build.sh
  source_path docs/experiences/civic-transparency/BRIEF.md
  source_path docs/experiences/civic-transparency/pages/ask.md
  source_path docs/experiences/civic-transparency/pages/search-logs.md
  source_path docs/experiences/civic-transparency/pages/sources.md
  source_path docs/experiences/civic-transparency/pages/fix.md
  source_path docs/experiences/presentations/civic-watch.json
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/civic_watch_site_test.sh
  witness cmd/BonfyreSourceFrontier/tests/civic_ledger_test.sh: 30 checks -- town dedupe and sort, county totals, ODbL attribution, refusal of a body carrying one position, of raw elements, of drifted bytes, of robots refusals, of non-200 reads and of unlicensed bodies; council dedupe, reader-only filter, first-line titles, JSON escape decoding, markup neutralised, unsafe GUID and host refused; reads table rows (2026-10-30)
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/civic_watch_site_test.sh with BONFYRE_TEST_WEB_BINARY from a scratch build: 39 checks -- build and idempotent rebuild through the site verbs, eight routes answer 200, presentation applied, starter post replaced, counts, record links and failed reads served, letter copyable, a contact-page correction reaches `site inbox` and is not published, no coordinate-like number and no machine vocabulary in visible text (2026-10-30)
  witness 2026-10-30 live ForeignTwin reads: Overpass at maps.mail.ru returned 154 town and 4 county totals (4,328 mapped readers across Dallas, Tarrant, Collin and Denton counties); overpass-api.de refused by robots and left alone; Legistar answered for Dallas (6 reader items), Fort Worth (8), McKinney (1) and Plano (0), and with 500 for Arlington, Irving, Garland, Frisco and Denton; headless Chrome screenshots of all eight routes at 1440 and 390 px
  known_gap not placed on any live host; the fixture host is watch.example.test and placement plus the edge publish path is the owner's step
  known_gap five Legistar clients answered 500 on the day of reading; cities on Granicus or CivicClerk need their own reader
  known_gap town counts depend on one Overpass mirror that answers 504 under load; the previous read is kept when it does
  known_gap the site kit renders the post author subject (institution:civic-watch) in hidden markup on the front page
  interacts foreign-twin
  interacts presentation-template

interaction foreign-twin-feeds-civic-transparency
  source foreign-twin
  destination civic-transparency
  relation receipted_public_record_projection
  preserves source URL, read time, robots decision, HTTP status, content digest, ODbL notice, city record identity and link
  drops camera positions (refused, never parsed), presenter lines, items that do not name a reader system, raw bodies
  forbidden_inference a ForeignTwin receipt -> the truth of what the source says; it is evidence the source said it at that time
  invalidates_on a new observation of the same source, or a body that no longer hashes to its receipt
  witness cmd/BonfyreSourceFrontier/tests/civic_ledger_test.sh
  binding cmd/BonfyreSourceFrontier/tools/civic_ledger.c

interaction civic-transparency-styled-by-presentation-template
  source civic-transparency
  destination presentation-template
  relation site_presentation_binding
  preserves the site's faces, palette, hero, navigation, density and card modes
  drops nothing of the page's content
  forbidden_inference a presentation -> a claim about the records the pages show
  invalidates_on `site set --presentation` with another file
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/civic_watch_site_test.sh
  binding docs/experiences/presentations/civic-watch.json
